. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2: Having daughters leads to more left-leaning politic
> al preferences *
. 
.         * Model: Fixed-effects linear regression (xtreg)
.         * Dependent variable = left-leaning attitudes (factorial score of plh
> 0016 - plh002)
.         * Independent variable: number of years with daughter(s)
.         * Control variables: age, education, life satisfaction, political int
> erest
. 
.         *xtset
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (strongly balanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2002 to 2017, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtsum age educ lifesat polint left_att_x ydaughters

